WEBVTT

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.250
A class 20 nuclear explosion
confirmed in Pilgrimage Point.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.880
Is Frank ever going to wake up again?

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.210
Will he open his eyes?

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:54.690
I don't know.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:59.440
But you helped Frank so many times before!

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.490
We're flying over ground zero now.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.860
Roger, how's the radiation?

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.060
Count 8, within NBC safety limits.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:44.240
Can you confirm any traces of the targets?

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.930
We're looking now.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.810
We won't find anything.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.570
That was an explosion of historic proportions.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.880
No matter how clean our laser signals are...

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.880
What's that?

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.120
A grave keeper?

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.720
That's what it looks like.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.060
The aliens protected her grave?

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.020
Perhaps at the last moment,
they redeemed themselves.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:49.060
While preserving some important
thought that wasn't lost yet.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.690
How is he?

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.700
He?

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.720
You mean Frank?

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.440
Or Yuri Leonov?

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.550
Either way, he hasn't spoken a word since.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:12.540
Such an ironic homecoming.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:18.020
Upon learning of the tragic reality,
he has closed his mind again.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.170
Romantic illusion, right?

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.560
Ma'am?

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:27.170
Words of contempt once said to
a man referring to his true heart...

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.230
Commander.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.850
I should have guessed.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.170
They're confiscating him now after all this?

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:59.480
With the alien threat over for now,

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.910
they just want to gather and burn the remains.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.680
There's no longer a reason to keep him alive.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:05.750
But...

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:06.910
Exactly.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.610
They haven't given the real reason.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.190
Or...

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.310
An evil intention without reason.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.130
Sometimes, when you reach a certain age,

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.260
all you can think about is your roses.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:27.760
I finally understand what the
brigadier general is all about.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:31.630
And what General Lawrence said, too.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:40.810
Take care of him.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:42.280
What about you?

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:44.880
I still have other business to attend to.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:51.090
"Good friend, for Jesus' sake forbear
to dig the dust enclosed here."

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.160
"Blessed be the man that spares these stones..."

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.600
"...and cursed be he that moves my bones."

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.710
That's what's engraved on Shakespeare's grave.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:07.800
Truth can be poison.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:10.780
You should heed its warning and keep away.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:12.400
Wait!

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.640
Why did you...

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:17.910
We'll meet again, Mr. Ryu Soma.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.970
Again?

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.260
What should we do, Captain?

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:31.420
Ma'am...

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:32.900
What's good?

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.540
What's evil?

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:37.260
What is the purpose to whatever we do?

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:41.040
And what is the consequence
after we conquer our duties?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:47.380
First of all, good and evil
don't exist in this world.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.150
I understand that.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.090
But take a look.

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:53.460
All this confusion.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:56.650
How are we supposed to think and behave?

00:07:58.560 --> 00:07:59.550
Well...

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.150
Well...

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.760
By being true to ourselves.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:11.730
I see.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.440
Defense level green.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.140
All units on alert.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:23.440
Ma'am.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.720
Release Hattie and Lt. Harris
from the jail at once.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.520
The mechanics, too.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.650
And disarm the security system.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.090
But...

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.400
I'm being true to myself, Captain.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.540
I don't get it.

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:51.980
I just don't get it.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.340
Maki...

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:54.410
Maki...

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.610
What am I supposed to do?

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.410
What should I do?

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:03.420
What should I...

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:05.080
Maki...

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:06.350
Maki...

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.920
What am I supposed to do?

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.930
Who am I?

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:13.990
Who...

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.940
Who am I?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.240
Takuto Kaneshiro.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.550
Dr. Noguchi's...

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.250
Right.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:36.120
His assistant and the only
survivor from the first Morgue.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.490
But why...

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.960
Many mysteries surround that incident.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:45.660
What's that?

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.900
It fell around the laboratory
where the EX-1 was.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.700
And the black SARG that attacked Ryu...

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:57.140
If it turns out the army's
TODs are the same design...

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:59.510
The truth can be harsh...

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.910
Please forgive me.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:44.820
No, it's too convenient to say
things like that now, isn't it?

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.160
You're free.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:53.270
If you can forgive me for
what I've done to you...

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.430
Your sins can never be forgiven!

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.680
You've disobeyed many orders.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:36.240
Misuse of troops.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.140
None of that is forgivable.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.180
Colonel Kilgore, you...

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.370
You have the wrong man.

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:49.150
Call me General Kilgore.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:53.390
You're rather heavily armed
for a confiscation procedure.

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.650
Sorry for the last-minute report.

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:58.130
Effective at 2300 hours today,

00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:01.800
Funeral is an official branch of the army.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:06.260
You are also relieved from
your post as commander.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:08.800
Here are the orders.

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.110
As you were.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.250
Can you hear me, control?

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.800
Commander, what's going on?

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:30.660
What's this transfer of facility order?

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:32.030
Later.

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:35.200
Put me through to General Wilson's office.

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.130
But...

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.810
An open channel is fine.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:38.870
Hurry.

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.340
We received a report.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:44.040
General Wilson died from
a heart attack two hours ago.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.180
Commander, can you hear me?

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:50.240
Commander?

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:58.060
It's too hard to believe.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.890
It's not an observation mistake?

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.900
The margin of error is less than 0.8%.

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:04.400
If this is true...

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:05.820
No!

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.560
Let's check again.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.230
This can't be.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.320
Frank...

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:33.380
Don't move!

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:36.670
Cut that out!

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.930
Pointing a gun at a child...

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:40.870
You call yourselves soldiers?

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:45.930
I finally found it.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.870
The gun that left this.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.440
The bullet found at Morgue?

00:13:57.890 --> 00:13:59.580
You know something?

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:03.350
Get on!

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:05.350
Do you, Captain?

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.030
Hey, hurry up!

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.720
We don't want to make our tour guides angry.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.730
Let's talk about it inside.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.770
All right?

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.860
Mr. Takuto Kaneshiro?

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:18.240
Where will they go?

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.840
For interrogation.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:23.050
At the base in Cleveland.
After that, I don't know.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:25.650
I don't see the need to take Harriet.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:26.780
This is your fault,

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:31.340
since you didn't report that the
EX-1 has gained consciousness.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:35.830
That girl's testimony is essential.

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:38.160
I have one question.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.130
How did you find out about Frank?

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:41.930
Despite being a female,

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:44.660
you've proven to be a capable commander.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:46.700
It's not just a compliment.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:50.140
But if there's one thing you could study more,

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:52.370
it would be human nature.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:54.830
Excuse me.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:56.810
Lt. Simmons?

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.220
He's been our eyes and ears.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:03.590
The lieutenant?

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:04.750
It can't be...

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:08.720
And the boy's made captain.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:12.850
Tell me, Dan.

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:16.430
Please tell me.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:17.720
Why?

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.000
I...

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:27.600
It's me.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:28.970
Put him through.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:30.430
I...

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.850
I just didn't want to lose.

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.080
Lose?

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:36.140
At what?

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:41.050
And have you won, Dan Simmons?

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:42.720
I was thinking...

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:45.760
I didn't want to be like my father;

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:49.470
another pencil pusher counting casualties all day.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:52.920
That's why I enlisted to be
where the real action was.

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.790
But it's all the same.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.870
No matter how capable you are,

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:01.760
you can die needlessly from
an inept superior's orders.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.410
I didn't want to die like a dog.

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:05.680
So that's why I...

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:06.670
Dan.

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:11.350
Was I an inept superior to you?

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.020
That's...

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.150
What?

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:15.590
8,000 kilometers?

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.060
Absurd!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:19.690
That's absurd!

00:16:19.690 --> 00:16:21.800
What's the projection?

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:23.630
Almost as big as the Earth...

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:24.700
No way!

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.660
It's the same every time!

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:28.660
What's the projected time?

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.210
The estimated time of arrival will be...

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:35.980
...97.324 hours.

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:37.940
Four more days...

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:39.710
Four more days until the Earth...

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:41.440
That's not the problem!

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.790
I-If it comes...

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:45.120
If it comes...

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:48.890
The moment it gets inside the Roche limit,

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:52.160
with its powerful magnetic
and gravitational pulls...

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:53.620
The Earth will...

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:09.740
They were afraid of the fact that the EX-1...

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:13.380
...Yuri Leonov, might gain consciousness.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.080
Either they originally planned this whole thing,

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:18.990
or they realized the secret of the aliens.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:21.460
Or it's an evil intention without reason.

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:22.890
In any event,

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:26.400
they tried to wipe out Frank by
sending TODs during the transport.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:29.730
They torched a whole village just to find a ring.

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:33.630
It all started with that incident at Morgue.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:38.670
Give me a break.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.810
Our enemies weren't just the aliens.

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:45.820
I even believed that he was one of us until now.

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:47.780
I don't think Dan's a part of it.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:51.790
At least he isn't the enemy.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:55.690
He just chose a different
path under his own beliefs.

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:57.760
How do you know that?

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:59.190
Just a feeling.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:02.700
I guess you know him better than we do.

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.340
Could that be jealousy?

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:05.730
Who's jealous?

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:23.280
Frank...

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:27.290
Will we ever see him again?

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.890
Don't worry, we will.

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:29.950
But...

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:33.250
I...

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.460
I always...

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:37.750
...wanted to kill him.

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.710
You mean Frank?

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:40.930
Right.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:43.380
H-Hold on, you...

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:45.600
I hated the one who killed Maki.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:49.100
That's why I changed my
name and joined Funeral.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:52.060
Yes, it was all for revenge.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:53.780
But...

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:55.350
That was an accident...

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:59.340
No, a miscalculation by
someone as human as you.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:02.070
So what will you do now?

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.460
I don't know.

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:05.260
Even I don't know what to do!

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:10.500
I've lost everything.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.100
I'm alone!

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:14.100
That's why I hated him.

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:15.500
But...

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:19.070
But he wasn't the one I should have hated!

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:22.130
Then who should I blame now?

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:23.540
Who should I kill?

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:31.290
I...

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:34.760
I lost the one I wanted to take revenge on.

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:36.430
He was just like me...

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:38.390
He forgot his own name...

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:41.490
The same pitiful human beings...

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:47.240
What am I supposed to do now?

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.670
What, Maki?

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:59.080
You were a bad fairy once, weren't you, Ryu?

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:02.740
But you helped Frank and me so many times.

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.590
You're a good fairy now.

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:08.460
You forgive me?

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:11.190
Even though I wanted to kill your Frank?

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:12.950
It's because...

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:17.130
It's because Frank's still alive.

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:19.130
Hattie...

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.170
Who?

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.170
Then Oberon, king of the fairies, sings...

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:38.990
"Be as thou wast wont to be."

00:20:38.990 --> 00:20:41.050
"See as thou wast wont to see."

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:45.650
"Dian's bud o'er Cupid's flower
hath such force and blessed power."

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.180
Look!

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:56.360
SARG 2.

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:58.070
Wh-Why?

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:03.740
My old guardian angel does have a magic wand.

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:06.750
I'm like you, Ryu.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:09.410
I'm here now because he guided me.

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:12.250
Look at that thing go!

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:16.990
He's inside the rays of the sun!

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.800
Former 2nd commander of the interplanetary fleet...

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.450
...Major General David Lawrence
hereby orders you!

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:28.930
Land the aircraft now!

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:33.370
Then abandon it, leaving all
five members of Funeral!

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:38.140
What's he doing?

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:40.940
To stay alive or perish forthwith.

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:45.450
You may tolerate the harsh reality of fate.

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:49.830
Or take out your own sword
and fight to end your suffering.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.960
Which do you think is nobler?

00:21:53.130 --> 00:21:55.630
This is the worst possible scenario that anyone could have imagined.

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:59.090
An 8,000 kilometer tall alien...

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:02.500
It brings the complete destruction of the world.

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.000
No, it can't be...

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:06.670
He's the only hope.

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:10.670
He's the only one who can
save us from this catastrophe!

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:35.010
Truth and Destruction

00:22:36.670 --> 00:22:38.540
Everything has been lost.

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:41.710
Only one thing remains in the empty hand.

00:22:41.910 --> 00:22:44.850
That is the lonely weapon called courage.

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:48.050
Next time,
Destruction and Courage.
